            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "deb az"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The video was very helpful. I made these using a nearly black plantain with 2T Coconut Oil in a non-stick frypan. I was using the dish for a dessert so mid-way through cooking I sprinkled on about 1T Brown Sugar and 1/4 teaspoon cinnamon. Near the end of cooking I lightly sprinkled with salt. The taste was good. I might fry them a little hotter next time to create a crispier exterior. \n\nNote: I would suggest not placing them on a paper towel lined plate as mine stuck to it! I am always in favor of trying to remove excess oil but will try a way other than a paper towel next time."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy Townsend Schroeder"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Main reason I gave it only 3 stars is that if recipe is followed, cooking them on high heat, they will burn. The instructions need to suggest a lower heat. We had to scrape off the burnt crust. The video instructs differently. Otherwise they are fabulous.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-08T23:40:10.847Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "fruitdog"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These got charred pretty quickly, so watch that. Just salted them and had them with black beans and rice too. They were still great, even with one side less than perfect. Will do again. I'm new to plantains, they take forever to darken. I tried that trick where you put a banana in a paper wine bag to ripen it faster, worked well for the plantains but took about a week to get it a nice color.",
            "datePublished": "2023-04-29T18:11:28.465Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sixtwentyseven"
            },
            "reviewBody": "First off -- please watch the video!!! \n\nI am not the most experienced at frying foods, so I decided to read the directions and follow them (literally) without watching the video. Rookie mistake.\n\nCooking this on high heat for 4-6 mins on each side will burn your plantains. If you watch the video, Chef John suggests using medium-high heat, I'd opt for medium heat. Also, keep an eye on the plantains and don't be afraid to turn them a few times to make sure they cook evenly and don't burn.\n\nTip: I followed another reviewers advice and added cinnamon while in the skillet (didn't have brown sugar, but will have that next time). Added the salt at the end. Took out the plantains and placed directly on a glass plate.",
            "datePublished": "2017-11-05T02:47:27.950Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Randy Pribbernow"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I picked plantains that were about half brown, noticed a flavor difference between slight color differences. Very unique flavor,I used grape seed oil, and got a mild sweet potato hint.",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-22T03:37:28.780Z"
